1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Your name is an equation. Follower number 1000 gets theirs.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,200
Part 1 — Tokenize.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,400
Give it a name. Take RANIA.

4
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,000
A model never sees the word. It cuts it into tokens first.

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A short name — one letter, one token.

6
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,600
Part 2 — Vectors.

7
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,600
a equals 1, b equals 2, all the way to z equals 26.

8
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,200
So RANIA becomes 18, 1, 14, 9, 1. Every token is just a number.

9
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,200
This is all a model ever holds. Now watch what the numbers can do.

10
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,800
Part 3 — Space x y.

11
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,800
Drop the numbers into x-y space. Each number becomes a wheel.

12
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,800
And the number is its speed — how fast that wheel turns.

13
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,400
Five numbers, one moving point.

14
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,000
Part 4 — Equation.

15
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,800
x of t is the sum of r-k times cosine of v-k t. y of t is the same with sine.

16
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,000
v is the letters: 18, 1, 14, 9, 1. r is the sizes: 1, a half, a third, a quarter, a fifth.

17
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,600
Every speed is a whole number, so the curve always closes. This one is RANIA.

18
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,200
SARA. Different letters, a different shape.

19
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,600
And back to RANIA. One name, one curve — nobody else has this one.

20
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,000
Follower number 1000 gets their name drawn like this. Comment your name.

21
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
